# Force LF line endings for everything text-based, regardless of the
# checking-out machine's core.autocrlf setting. This matters well beyond
# style: src-tauri/migrations/*.sql gets embedded verbatim into the compiled
# binary via include_str!(), and Tauri's migration runner (sqlx underneath)
# checksums that exact byte content against what's already recorded in an
# existing local database. A GitHub Actions Windows runner defaults to
# autocrlf=true, so without this file, a fresh checkout there converts LF to
# CRLF, silently changing every migration's bytes and its checksum — any
# database that already recorded "migration 1 applied" against the LF
# version (e.g. from a locally-built dev copy, or any earlier release) would
# then fail to open with "migration N was previously applied but has been
# modified" against the CRLF-checksummed CI build. Pinning LF here makes the
# embedded bytes identical no matter which OS or autocrlf setting checked
# the repo out.
* text=auto eol=lf
